## Extracted recovery ramdisk

The selected stock recovery payload is extracted once and reused directly.

- **recovery/stock-root/** contains the complete expanded selected recovery
  payload in the generation workspace for audit and for recovering extra device
  files. Cloud/export ZIPs omit it by default unless stock-root inclusion was
  explicitly requested.
- **recovery/root/** is the build overlay consumed by Android/TWRP.
- **recovery/ramdisk-manifest.json** records the selected image or fragment and
  the entries copied into both trees.
- **recovery.stock.fstab** preserves the exact stock fstab used as input.
  **recovery.fstab** is the normalized TWRP-oriented output; compare the two
  before building because formatter-visible flags are not guaranteed to cover
  every stock fs_mgr detail.

{% if recovery_root_mode == "full" %}
Full mode was explicitly requested, so the complete selected recovery payload
is also placed in recovery/root. This can replace files supplied by TWRP and
should only be used when that exact overlay is intended.
{% else %}
Auto/minimal mode keeps the complete extraction in stock-root but seeds only
device-specific init, vendor/odm, firmware/module and VINTF content into
recovery/root. This applies to typed RECOVERY fragments too, preventing stock
recovery, stock init, adbd and generic system files from replacing TWRP's own
recovery implementation.
{% endif %}

