## Mandatory verification before building

1. Provisional partition-size limits were derived from input image file sizes,
   rounded UP to 4 KiB. These are NOT verified physical partition capacities.
   Compare all against stock GPT/lpdump before flashing; custom TWRP may exceed
   the original image length. Verified --boot-size/--recovery-size take priority.
2. Confirm recovery placement and the target TWRP branch's vendor_boot/init_boot
   build flags. Extraction support does not make repacking device-independent.
3. Check ramdisk fragment selection, DTB/DTBO, fstab block devices, slot suffixes,
   logical partitions, filesystem formats, and encryption dependencies.
4. Reconcile stock AVB signing and rollback rules. Do not blindly disable AVB.
5. Check SELinux policy, kernel modules, vendor HALs, input/display and
   decryption services before trusting recovery on a physical phone.
6. Confirm the build target with the chosen branch's lunch list.

{% if device_info.manufacturer == "samsung" and recovery_layout == "dedicated" %}
7. Samsung dedicated-recovery devices may require a device-specific image
   trailer, Odin tar packaging, or verified-boot handling. NEXT does not invent
   those rules from the manufacturer name; compare the stock/known-good image
   packaging before flashing.
{% endif %}

